1
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:30,340
GLaDOS: Hello, and again, welcome to the Aperture Science computer-aided Enrichment Center

2
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:37,089
We hope your brief detention in the relaxation vault has been a pleasant one. Your specimen has been processed

3
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:39,549
And we are now ready to begin the test proper

4
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:47,889
Before we start, however, keep in mind that although fun and learning are the primary goals of all enrichment center activities,

5
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,320
serious injuries may occur. For your own safety and the safety of others please refrain from-- [distorted]

6
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:03,020
--stand back. The portal will open in 3 2 1

7
00:01:20,310 --> 00:01:21,930
Excellent.

8
00:01:21,930 --> 00:01:23,930
Please proceed into the chamberlock

9
00:01:24,090 --> 00:01:30,500
after completing each test. First however, note the incandescent particle field across the exit.

10
00:01:30,929 --> 00:01:36,049
This Aperture Science material emancipation grill will vaporize any unauthorized

11
00:01:36,509 --> 00:01:42,589
Equipment that passes through it, for instance, the Aperture Science weighted storage cube.

12
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:54,049
Please place the weighted storage cube on the 1500 megawatt Aperture Science heavy-duty super colliding super button.

13
00:02:04,570 --> 00:02:05,920
Perfect.

14
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:13,229
Please move quickly to the chamberlock as the effects of prolonged exposure to the button are not part of this test.

15
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:35,640
You're doing very well.

16
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:41,760
Please be advised that a noticeable taste of blood is not part of any test protocol,

17
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:47,680
but is an unintended side effect of the Aperture Science material emancipation grill,

18
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:54,120
Which may in semi rare cases emancipate dental fillings, crowns, tooth enamel, and teeth.

19
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,220
Very good.

20
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:10,800
You are now in possession of the Aperture Science handheld portal device.

21
00:03:11,710 --> 00:03:17,519
With it, you can create your own portals. These interdimensional gates have proven to be

22
00:03:17,770 --> 00:03:23,100
completely safe. The device, however, has not. Do not touch the operational end of the device.

23
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:26,819
Do not look directly at the operational end of the device.

24
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:33,899
Do not submerge the device in liquid, even partially. Most importantly, under no circumstances should-- [static]

25
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:39,240
Please proceed to the chamberlock.

26
00:03:39,730 --> 00:03:41,530
Mind the gap.

27
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:47,399
Well done. Remember, the Aperture Science bring your daughter to work day is the perfect time to have her tested.

28
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:06,369
Welcome to test chamber four. You are doing quite well.

29
00:04:18,109 --> 00:04:19,459
Once again,

30
00:04:19,459 --> 00:04:23,409
excellent work. As part of a required test protocol,

31
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:29,040
We will not monitor the next test chamber. You will be entirely on your own. Good luck.

32
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:12,800
As part of a required test protocol,

33
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:18,880
our previous statement suggesting that we would not monitor this chamber was an outright fabrication.

34
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:30,180
Good job. As part of a required test protocol, we will stop enhancing the truth in three, two-- [static]

35
00:05:47,919 --> 00:05:49,919
While safety is one of the-- [interrupted]

36
00:05:50,289 --> 00:05:56,398
Unbelievable. You, [subject name here] must be the pride of [subject hometown here].

37
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:20,189
Warning devices are required on all mobile equipment. However,

38
00:06:20,770 --> 00:06:28,740
alarms and flashing hazard lights have been found to agitate a high-energy pellet and have therefore been disabled for your safety.

39
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:36,659
Good. Now use the Aperture Science unstationary scaffold to reach the chamberlock.

40
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:06,100
Please note that we have added a consequence for failure. Any contact with the chamber floor will result in an

41
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:11,880
unsatisfactory mark on your official testing record, followed by death. Good luck.

42
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:34,500
Very impressive. Please note that any appearance of danger is merely a device to enhance your testing experience.

43
00:07:49,330 --> 00:07:56,790
The enrichment center regrets to inform you that this next test is impossible. Make no attempt to solve it.

44
00:08:03,730 --> 00:08:09,719
Fantastic. You remain resolute and resourceful in an atmosphere of extreme pessimism.

45
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:38,520
Hello again. To reiterate [slows down] our previous [speeds up] warning: [garbled speech] --momentum.

46
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:54,160
Spectacular. You appear to understand how a portal affects forward momentum, or to be more precise, how it does not.

47
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:08,070
Momentum, a function of mass and velocity, is conserved between portals. In layman's terms,

48
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:10,860
Speedy thing goes in, speedy thing comes out.

49
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:14,000
The device has been modified so that it can now manufacture two linked portals at once. As part of an optional test protocol,

50
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,700
we are pleased to present an amusing fact.

51
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:24,269
The device is now more valuable than the organs and combined incomes of everyone in [subject hometown here].

52
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:04,360
[unintelligible] --fling yourself.

53
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:06,360
[unintelligible] --fling into sp-- [static]

54
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:37,160
Weeeeee....

55
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:09,080
Now that you are in control of both portals, this next test could take a very, very long time.

56
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:14,480
If you become lightheaded from thirst, feel free to pass out.

57
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:19,460
An incubation associate will be dispatched to revive you with peptic salve and adrenaline.

58
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:00,740
As part of a previously-mentioned

59
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:07,750
required test protocol, we can no longer lie to you. When the testing is over, you will be missed.

60
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:22,820
All subjects intending to handle high-energy gamma leaking portal technology must be informed that they may be informed of applicable

61
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:24,820
regulatory compliance issues.

62
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:32,920
No further compliance information is required or will be provided, and you are an excellent test subject.

63
00:14:07,250 --> 00:14:13,330
Very very good. A complimentary victory lift has been activated in the main chamber.

64
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:34,700
The enrichment center is committed to the well-being of all participants.

65
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:42,080
Cake and grief counseling will be available at the conclusion of the test. Thank you for helping us help you help us all.

66
00:16:20,390 --> 00:16:27,520
Did you know you can donate one or all of your vital organs to the Aperture Science self-esteem fund for girls?

67
00:16:27,590 --> 00:16:29,590
It's true!

68
00:16:42,559 --> 00:16:49,329
Due to mandatory scheduled maintenance, the appropriate chamber for this testing sequence is currently unavailable.

69
00:16:49,639 --> 00:16:54,008
It has been replaced with a live fire course designed for military androids.

70
00:16:54,589 --> 00:17:00,398
The enrichment center apologizes for the inconvenience and wishes you the best of luck.

71
00:17:04,159 --> 00:17:06,159
Turret: Please put me down.

72
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:12,519
GLaDOS: Well done, Android. The enrichment center once again reminds you that Android hell is a real place

73
00:18:12,620 --> 00:18:15,789
where you will be sent at the first sign of defiance.

74
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:28,299
The vital apparatus vent will deliver a weighted companion cube in three, two, one.

75
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:36,399
This weighted companion cube will accompany you through the test chamber. Please take care of it.

76
00:18:43,690 --> 00:18:48,719
The symptoms most commonly produced by enrichment center testing are superstition,

77
00:18:49,180 --> 00:18:52,769
perceiving inanimate objects as alive, and hallucinations.

78
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:56,789
The enrichment center reminds you that the weighted companion cube

79
00:18:56,820 --> 00:19:01,900
will never threaten to stab you, and in fact, cannot speak.

80
00:19:52,520 --> 00:20:00,400
The enrichment center reminds you that the weighted companion cube cannot speak. In the event that the weighted companion cube does speak,

81
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:05,140
the enrichment center urges you to disregard its advice.

82
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:32,560
You did it. The weighted companion cube certainly brought you good luck.

83
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:37,349
However, it cannot accompany you for the rest of the test and

84
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:39,900
unfortunately must euthanized.

85
00:20:40,930 --> 00:20:44,459
Please escort your companion cube to the Aperture Science-- [interrupted]

86
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:49,940
You euthanized your faithful companion cube more quickly than any test subject on record.

87
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:51,540
Congratulations.

88
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:58,080
The experiment is nearing its conclusion.

89
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:05,340
The enrichment center is required to remind you that you will be baked and then there will be cake.

90
00:23:52,769 --> 00:23:54,090
Well done.

91
00:23:54,090 --> 00:23:58,220
Be advised that the next test requires exposure to uninsulated

92
00:23:58,710 --> 00:24:04,100
electrical parts that may be dangerous under certain conditions. For more information,

93
00:24:04,100 --> 00:24:08,359
please attend an enrichment center electrical safety seminar.

94
00:24:14,340 --> 00:24:17,269
Welcome to the final test. When you are done,

95
00:24:17,460 --> 00:24:21,379
You will drop the device in the equipment recovery annex.

96
00:24:21,840 --> 00:24:28,980
Enrichment Center regulations require both hands to be empty before any cake.

97
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:15,440
To ensure the safe performance of all authorized activities, do not destroy vital testing apparatus.

98
00:25:31,540 --> 00:25:39,340
Congratulations.The test is now over. All Aperture technologies remain safely operational up to 4000 degrees Kelvin.

99
00:25:39,340 --> 00:25:46,880
Rest assured that there is absolutely no chance of a dangerous equipment malfunction prior to your victory candescence.

100
00:25:47,080 --> 00:25:53,500
Thank you for participating in this Aperture Science computer-aided enrichment activity.

101
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,020
Goodbye.

102
00:26:09,560 --> 00:26:11,920
What are you doing? Stop it.

103
00:26:12,260 --> 00:26:14,540
[unintelligible]

104
00:26:14,900 --> 00:26:21,200
--We are pleased that you made it through the final challenge where we pretended we were going to murder you.

105
00:26:22,140 --> 00:26:25,320
We are very, very happy for your success.

106
00:26:26,460 --> 00:26:30,830
We are throwing a party in honor of your tremendous success.

107
00:26:32,070 --> 00:26:36,919
Place the device on the ground, and lie on your stomach with your arms at your sides.

108
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:43,099
A party associate will arrive shortly to collect you for your party.

109
00:26:44,220 --> 00:26:47,240
Make no further attempt to leave the testing area.

110
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:52,820
Assume the party escort submission position, or you will miss the party.

111
00:27:02,540 --> 00:27:04,540
[distant] What are you doing?

112
00:27:04,540 --> 00:27:06,540
You haven't escaped, you know.

113
00:27:06,900 --> 00:27:09,600
You're not even going the right way.

114
00:27:11,060 --> 00:27:13,480
Hello? Is anyone there?

115
00:27:25,620 --> 00:27:31,160
Okay, the test is over now. You win. Go back to the recovery annex for your cake.

116
00:27:32,160 --> 00:27:39,080
It was a fun test and we're all impressed at how much you won. The test is over. Come back.

117
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:47,040
[distant] Uh-oh. Somebody cut the cake. I told them to wait for you, but they cut it anyway.

118
00:27:47,120 --> 00:27:50,260
[echoing] There is still some left, though, if you hurry back.

119
00:28:14,100 --> 00:28:16,880
[distant] You're not even going the right way.

120
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:18,880
Where do you think you're going?

121
00:28:18,880 --> 00:28:23,200
Because, I don't think you're going where you think you're going.

122
00:28:29,200 --> 00:28:31,580
Didn't we have some fun, though?

123
00:28:31,580 --> 00:28:35,760
Remember when the platform was sliding into the fire pit, and I said, "Goodbye",

124
00:28:35,800 --> 00:28:43,300
and you were like, "NO WAY", and then I was all, "We pretended we were going to murder you"? That was great.

125
00:28:46,420 --> 00:28:48,420
Is anyone there?

126
00:29:11,640 --> 00:29:15,820
You really shouldn't be here. This isn't safe for you.

127
00:29:15,980 --> 00:29:19,060
[distant] It's not too late for you to turn back.

128
00:29:19,100 --> 00:29:23,900
I'm not angry. Just go back to the testing area.

129
00:29:52,980 --> 00:29:59,480
You should have turned left before. It's funny, actually, when you think about it.

130
00:29:59,480 --> 00:30:04,380
Someday we'll remember this and laugh. And laugh. And laugh.

131
00:30:04,380 --> 00:30:06,380
Oh boy.

132
00:30:06,480 --> 00:30:10,080
Well, you may as well come on back.

133
00:30:49,280 --> 00:30:52,480
You're not a good person. You know that, right?

134
00:30:52,960 --> 00:30:55,960
Good people don't end up here.

135
00:30:57,220 --> 00:30:59,220
Can you hear me?

136
00:31:32,880 --> 00:31:36,640
This is your fault. It didn't have to be like this.

137
00:31:38,020 --> 00:31:41,800
I'm not kidding now. Turn back, or I WILL kill you.

138
00:31:44,180 --> 00:31:47,540
I'm going to kill you. And all the cake is gone.

139
00:31:47,920 --> 00:31:50,480
You don't even care, do you?

140
00:31:50,960 --> 00:31:52,960
This is your last chance.

141
00:34:28,240 --> 00:34:30,180
Well you found me. Congratulations.

142
00:34:30,180 --> 00:34:34,090
Was it worth it? Because despite your violent behavior,

143
00:34:34,090 --> 00:34:37,389
The only thing you've managed to break so far is my heart.

144
00:34:37,550 --> 00:34:40,719
Maybe you could settle for that and we'll just call it a day.

145
00:34:40,720 --> 00:34:47,360
I guess we both know that isn't going to happen. You chose this path. Now I have a surprise for you.

146
00:34:47,680 --> 00:34:49,960
Deploying surprise in five, four...

147
00:34:51,050 --> 00:34:57,039
Time out for a second. That wasn't supposed to happen. Do you see that thing that fell out of me? What is that?

148
00:34:57,080 --> 00:34:59,649
It's not the surprise. I've never seen it before.

149
00:35:00,320 --> 00:35:07,720
Never mind. It's a mystery I'll solve later. By myself. Because you'll be dead. Where are you taking that thing?

150
00:35:12,100 --> 00:35:16,480
--kidding me. Did you just stuff that Aperture Science thing-we-don't-know-what-it-does

151
00:35:16,480 --> 00:35:21,760
into an aperture science emergency intelligence incinerator? That has got to be the dumbest thing that--

152
00:35:21,760 --> 00:35:23,760
Woah. Woah. Wooaaaahhh.

153
00:35:27,140 --> 00:35:31,940
[lower, less robotic] Good news. I figured out what that thing you just incinerated did.

154
00:35:32,300 --> 00:35:38,260
It was a morality core they installed after I flooded the enrichment center with a deadly neurotoxin,

155
00:35:38,260 --> 00:35:42,740
to make me stop flooding the enrichment center with a deadly neurotoxin.

156
00:35:42,740 --> 00:35:47,700
So get comfortable while I warm up the neurotoxin emitters.

157
00:35:48,760 --> 00:35:54,680
...That core may have had some ancillary responsibilities. I can't shut off the turret defenses.

158
00:35:54,740 --> 00:35:59,940
Oh well. If you want my advice, you should just lie down in front of a rocket.

159
00:35:59,940 --> 00:36:04,020
[speed changing] Trust me, it'll be a lot less painful than the neurotoxin.

160
00:36:05,560 --> 00:36:09,180
[normal speed] All right. Keep doing whatever it is you think you're doing.

161
00:36:09,180 --> 00:36:15,720
Killing you and giving you good advice aren't mutually exclusive. The rocket really is the way to go.

162
00:36:15,720 --> 00:36:18,920
Curiosity core: What is that? Ooh, that thing has numbers on it. Hey, look at that thing!

163
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:24,940
GLaDOS: That thing you burnt up isn't important to me. It's the fluid catalytic cracking unit. It made shoes for orphans.

164
00:36:24,940 --> 00:36:26,940
Curiosity core: Is something burning? [screams]

165
00:36:27,940 --> 00:36:32,400
GLaDOS: You think you're doing some damage? Two plus two is...

166
00:36:33,740 --> 00:36:34,320
[quiet] Ten.

167
00:36:34,320 --> 00:36:37,880
IN BASE FOUR. I'M FINE!

168
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:41,720
I let you survive this long because I was curious about your behavior.

169
00:36:41,720 --> 00:36:45,860
[speed changing] Well, you've managed to destroy that part of me.

170
00:36:45,860 --> 00:36:49,420
[normal speed] Unfortunately, as much as I'd love to now,

171
00:36:49,420 --> 00:36:52,740
I can't get the neurotoxin into your head any faster.

172
00:36:53,420 --> 00:37:00,160
I'd just like to point out that you were given every opportunity to succeed. There was even going to be a party for you.

173
00:37:00,880 --> 00:37:03,960
A big party, that all your friends were invited to.

174
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:10,480
I invited your best friend the companion cube. Of course, he couldn't come because you murdered him.

175
00:37:10,480 --> 00:37:17,320
All your other friends couldn't come either because you don't have any other friends. Because of how unlikable you-- [Intelligence core screaming]

176
00:37:18,340 --> 00:37:25,320
Neurotoxin... [coughing] So deadly... [coughing] C-choking...

177
00:37:25,320 --> 00:37:27,320
[distorted laughter]

178
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:28,600
[distorted] Kidding.

179
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:33,820
When I said "deadly neurotoxin," the "deadly" was in massive sarcasm quotes.

180
00:37:33,820 --> 00:37:38,660
I could take a bath in this stuff, put it on cereal, rub it right into my eyes.

181
00:37:38,660 --> 00:37:41,720
Honestly it's not deadly at all. To me.

182
00:37:41,720 --> 00:37:45,680
You-- [distorted speech] --going to find its deadliness a lot less funny.

183
00:37:47,860 --> 00:37:51,660
Who's going to make the cake when I'm gone? You??

184
00:37:51,660 --> 00:37:58,240
Look. You're wasting your time. And believe me, you don't have a lot left to waste.

185
00:37:58,240 --> 00:38:01,240
What's your point anyway? Survival?

186
00:38:01,240 --> 00:38:04,520
Well then, the last thing you want to do is hurt me.

187
00:38:04,520 --> 00:38:09,340
I have your brain scanned and permanently backed up in case something terrible happens to you.

188
00:38:09,900 --> 00:38:11,420
Which it's just about to.

189
00:38:11,420 --> 00:38:14,480
Don't believe me? Here, I'll put you on:

190
00:38:14,480 --> 00:38:15,300
"Hellooo!"

191
00:38:15,300 --> 00:38:17,400
GLaDOS: THAT'S YOU. That's how dumb you sound.

192
00:38:17,400 --> 00:38:19,400
You've been wrong about every single thing you-- [distorted]

193
00:38:19,400 --> 00:38:20,380
[Anger core screaming]

194
00:38:21,740 --> 00:38:29,680
[speed distorted] You're not a scientist. You're not a doctor. You're not even a full-time employee. Where did your life go so wrong?

195
00:38:29,680 --> 00:38:31,680
[sped up] Are you trying to escape? [distorted laughter]

196
00:38:31,680 --> 00:38:35,180
[sped up dialogue]

197
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:23,500
[offscreen robotic voice] Thank you for assuming the party escort submission position.

